{"title":"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_May_2025)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, May 2025)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_with_gaps_filled_in\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution with gaps filled in</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e867843e87fa1fb7c6154599cd743d3446b798e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e6dc61f27fd585acc8e101875573214e7d1eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1}, \\overrightarrow{OP_2},\\cdots, \\overrightarrow{OP_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"153\" height=\"25\" /> are unit vectors such that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa050d186a773cb376da9c42302cf3058026ce64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, \\cdots, P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> all lie in a plane containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and on one side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6dc3c1362b8ec95b7e5fd733ee15d949286c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c261196979f62bc5b704df4bace1553f2760e4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left|\\overrightarrow{OP_1}+\\overrightarrow{OP_2}+\\cdots+ \\overrightarrow{OP_n}\\right|\\ge1.\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"34\" /> Here <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/8415b5bf277faaade60c89f90007d8b365ef2baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\overrightarrow{OM}\\right|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" /> denotes the length of vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197c8cf5d617dae42afd8e18c385159599558097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OM}.$\" width=\"37\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We prove it by induction on the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639e85fa2f2bb450812e9c9de2067851e11a04d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> of vectors. The base step (when we have one vector) is clear, and for the induction step we use the hypothesis for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f9a96c63183be91b9fe70e6e16dfa4bfec6f3da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> vectors obtained by disregarding the outermost two vectors. We thus get a vector with norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeac561619dcee65a2b45d737a79892aa0ebf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> betwen two with norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the two vectors of norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> makes an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b7f1e6cc52699faa67419e6b3fd62a121d9a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le\\frac\\pi 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"32\" height=\"33\" /> with the vector of norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeac561619dcee65a2b45d737a79892aa0ebf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />, so their sum has norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeac561619dcee65a2b45d737a79892aa0ebf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />, and we're done.\n</p><p>The above solution was posted and copyrighted by grobber. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p357939\">[1]</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_May_2025.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_May_2025)\">Remarks (added by pf02, May 2025)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, May 2025)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The \"solution\" given above is somewhat incomplete.  It simply\nshoves the difficulty of the problem into the phrase \"... so their\nsum has norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeac561619dcee65a2b45d737a79892aa0ebf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />, and we're done.\"  Indeed, while true, this\nis not obvious, and it needs a proof.\n</p><p>Below, I will fill in the gaps in the first \"solution\".  Then,\nI will give two more solutions.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_with_gaps_filled_in\">Solution with gaps filled in</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution with gaps filled in\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a0d6752fa4635fa677be613d74336bad140b8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />.  We give a proof by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/84574de7797bc7b4e1fc52075f4d265ba60a8bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we have one vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4b9c1f5ddf083a92bfa20138277ec5ccf8d465f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"24\" /> whose\nnorm (i.e. length) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we are done.\n</p><p>Assume the statement is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/2/8d287e24e7a1382cff2df773c0fbf3c3990c6006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, \\dots, k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> and prove\nthat it is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.  For ease of visualization, assume the\nplane to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> axes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fe60729c37515dec723a57cf2ac0c6c5ce369e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O = (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460dce80925c74b24846b78ecf9505ac5edeb4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />.  Assume the vectors are determined\nby <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fac363e91d2b3dc70e19a56553f8725c0d8a48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i = (\\cos \\alpha_i, \\sin \\alpha_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />, such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fcd72c39412079aea2076fed8fedb30a450a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\alpha_1 \\le \\alpha_2 \\le \\dots \\le \\alpha_n &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8a9adc3626a3da4b348155cbb5bac21bf43cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 = P_1, Q_3 = P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83bf0891a57ba8a1ee68d8c72f141ccbc14186d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> be determined by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58b186a887837f31373875357c381187ad174425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_2} = \\overrightarrow{OP_2} + \\dots + \\overrightarrow{OP_{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"25\" />\n(like in the solution above).  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91208728d1763347386ff67aa1f4800d275f7c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"24\" /> is the\nsum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18a1a0dce3c2605337d2bf3a3b5f39106a68be19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 2 = 2k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" /> unit vectors on one side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, its norm\nis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0aeac561619dcee65a2b45d737a79892aa0ebf8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> (because of the induction hypothesis).  Let us say that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/5013758605daa77a1edf32e1616fb1350883122f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2 = (a \\cos \\beta, a \\sin \\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />.  We want to show that the norm\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f72436ea42de26ace92119a429eadeaa6a5b285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_2} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3} \\right| \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76e0528adf3da89dbbbf0cc192370d306fb9fec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_1}, \\overrightarrow{OQ_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"24\" /> are unit vectors\nwhose angles with the positive direction of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis are\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67f2340e51127ee72807cc986f753b701cb1dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\alpha_1 \\le \\alpha_n &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"17\" /> the direction of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/79150d23c4b9fb2e3e1f9b427dfa4849dfdb71b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/33560f7bf360899a271b797690c2be6de65b45b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\alpha_1 + \\alpha_n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"37\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbb463dd6b83e3837058d5a76fc09aad4f8631f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha_1 \\le \\beta \\le \\alpha_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />, the angle between\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/79150d23c4b9fb2e3e1f9b427dfa4849dfdb71b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91208728d1763347386ff67aa1f4800d275f7c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"24\" />\nis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e50348a666f2211a7e494b1d763729b524f59a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Now use that the norm of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91208728d1763347386ff67aa1f4800d275f7c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"24\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/4/d644bfba7a125eab0feb6f52761c803a0215255e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, and the\ngeneral fact that if the angle between two vectors\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522c2f94142f120935d7c10a2dd1cc905d1e742a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{u}, \\overrightarrow{v}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e50348a666f2211a7e494b1d763729b524f59a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"34\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/3/6133ad81b68088357d0cfbb4b320a7683ad0a96a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\overrightarrow{u} + \\overrightarrow{v} \\right| \\ge \\max \\{ \\left| \\overrightarrow{u} \\right|, \\left| \\overrightarrow{v} \\right| \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/88205ae06ae82723fd34202bbd755d2fae5eee0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_2} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3} \\right| = \\left| (\\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3}) + \\overrightarrow{OQ_2} \\right| \\ge \\max \\left\\{ \\left| \\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3} \\right|, a \\right\\} \\ge a \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"649\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>To finish the proof, let us show this general fact about \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522c2f94142f120935d7c10a2dd1cc905d1e742a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{u}, \\overrightarrow{v}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> forming an angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e50348a666f2211a7e494b1d763729b524f59a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"34\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13e9a90ec00aab55d572329394285227c2340b69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{u} = \\overrightarrow{OA}, \\overrightarrow{v} = \\overrightarrow{OB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"24\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fda69b819aa12e67f57ecc772f3604386787ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{u} + \\overrightarrow{v} = \\overrightarrow{OC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be the lengths of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb034834a496809f1b968374dab1bf2d004b432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA, OB, OC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />.  Consider\nthe triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f541172f75246197371d1b6d5e3431b26f5796f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />.  The cosine formula in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f541172f75246197371d1b6d5e3431b26f5796f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAC$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />\nyields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec7845985a6ff7bfc4f536a8c6699a743342513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab\\cos C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"187\" height=\"16\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4056d41f42aa8a00adca0ff5d1209b6bb0e92d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is\nobtuse, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcfb9197d6d9d8c72c81bf11db3c4e046d9a151c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos C \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3bc1c66267a3871797fae495e44a34b5285644c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^2 \\ge a^2 + b^2 \\ge \\max \\{a^2, b^2\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"21\" />.\nThis implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7cb103f9c978f3c1de0fbcb950d67fadd30942c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\ge \\max \\{ a, b \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution starts exactly like the previous one, till the line\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/5013758605daa77a1edf32e1616fb1350883122f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_2 = (a \\cos \\beta, a \\sin \\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />.  We want to show that the norm\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f72436ea42de26ace92119a429eadeaa6a5b285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_2} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3} \\right| \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"200\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Then, we continue as follows:\n</p><p>The end point of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca43e7ec7e56159309da8baafe1957ee0befe49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_2} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3} = (\\cos \\alpha_1 + a \\cos \\beta + \\cos \\alpha_n, \\sin \\alpha_1 + a \\sin \\beta + \\sin \\alpha_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"576\" height=\"25\" />,\nand the square of the norm of this vector is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/6/d76d149066464b114c0e56d12460931341553d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\alpha_n, \\beta, a) = (\\cos \\alpha_1 + a \\cos \\beta + \\cos \\alpha_n)^2 + (\\sin \\alpha_1 + a \\sin \\beta + \\sin \\alpha_n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"577\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>After some computations, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f35e1b51baf0d0784ba1911880c73b064ac744c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\alpha_n, \\beta, a) = 2 + a^2 + 2a\\cos (\\alpha_n - \\beta) + 2a\\cos (\\beta - \\alpha_1) + 2\\cos (\\alpha_n - \\alpha_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"592\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> is a decreasing function from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> on the interval\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a151f5b93ce5735f72cdd79c46051f52b9d820d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b4b3edf20ceab0eabcc1e2026c7d5692f14e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\alpha_n, \\beta, a) \\ge S(0, \\pi, \\beta, a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e47d1816ec39099cfafe5a1f75fbb851785944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\alpha_n, \\beta, a) \\ge 2 + a^2 + 2a\\cos (\\pi - \\beta) + 2a\\cos (\\beta) + 2\\cos (\\pi) = a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"531\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that the norm\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792d8e47db5d8fb7cc70bb6f00fb3d7ed8c320c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\overrightarrow{OQ_1} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_2} + \\overrightarrow{OQ_3} \\right| \\ge a \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"234\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, May 2025]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For ease of visualization, assume the plane to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> axes,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fe60729c37515dec723a57cf2ac0c6c5ce369e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O = (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />.  Assume the\nvectors are determined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fac363e91d2b3dc70e19a56553f8725c0d8a48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i = (\\cos \\alpha_i, \\sin \\alpha_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />,\nsuch that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fcd72c39412079aea2076fed8fedb30a450a94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; \\alpha_1 \\le \\alpha_2 \\le \\dots \\le \\alpha_n &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>We are asked to show that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/1/b0181d85bb443da117fa22f5bfa3030802f2da69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left| \\sum_{i=1}^n \\overrightarrow{OP_i} \\right| \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"107\" height=\"55\" />.  Before\nembarking on the computations which prove this inequality, let\nus give the idea of the proof.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460dce80925c74b24846b78ecf9505ac5edeb4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />.  We will prove\nformally that by \"moving\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1db9c4378168d9624656cfb533120ce4361714c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> to their limiting positions\non <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> (i.e. replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754e946d1a160f767f0f61cbd9460401c2d1c17f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2671c3350cb05610366963fe0cb7fb94293b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />)\nthe norm of the sum of vectors will be decreased.  Repeat this\nargument for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b822a181e4857b295f3317b29217e46744ee130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2, P_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, etc. (for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> times).  We\nare left with one vector (the middle vector), which has norm <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\nNow let us turn this idea into a formal proof.\n</p><p>The point determining the sum of vectors is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc952d6ed3b8201ad286878dec5e5e79cbc85dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = (\\sum_{i=1}^n \\cos \\alpha_i, \\sum_{i=1}^n \\sin \\alpha_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"207\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>The square of the norm of the sum of vectors is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a861d17d5d0f967c3e7cf9a4dee434f64b9029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) = \\left| \\overrightarrow{OP} \\right|^2 = \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n \\cos \\alpha_i \\right)^2 + \\left( \\sum_{i=1}^n \\sin \\alpha_i \\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"442\" height=\"58\" />.\n</p><p>After some computations, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/e/67ec9e53ee99a5cac6ae5ac9fb19f0f57dde090b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) = n + 2 \\sum_{1 \\le i &lt; j \\le n} \\cos (\\alpha_j - \\alpha_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"334\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Denote\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff61540e9fc5a44fdf7470268a01cf7df399fab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) = 2 \\sum_{1 \\le i &lt; j \\le n} \\cos (\\alpha_j - \\alpha_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"302\" height=\"45\" />.\nWhen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbd52cbb130359b57f12c7f94e150262842a4d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(\\alpha_1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />.  (This makes sense both formally, and\nas an accommodation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/991226951062ad838dcf152f3910fef7d3478a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />.)\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b186a49225b1d1ccc8b1fe0d0dbe7a5144deef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) = 2 \\cos (\\alpha_n - \\alpha_1) + 2 \\sum_{1 &lt; i &lt; n} \\cos (\\alpha_n - \\alpha_i) + 2 \\sum_{1 &lt; j &lt; n} \\cos (\\alpha_j - \\alpha_1) + 2 \\sum_{2 \\le i &lt; j \\le n-1} \\cos (\\alpha_j - \\alpha_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"807\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> is a decreasing function from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> on the interval\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a151f5b93ce5735f72cdd79c46051f52b9d820d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa2b02ffc894c630ee60ad96f8e105391c7d182e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\dots, \\alpha_{n-1}, \\alpha_n) \\ge T(0, \\alpha_2, \\dots, \\alpha_{n-1}, \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"367\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d68665e9e0683a9727c636f1a2c8479e853b3d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(0, \\alpha_2, \\dots, \\alpha_{n-1}, \\pi) = 2 \\cos (\\pi - 0) + 2 \\sum_{1 &lt; i &lt; n} \\cos (\\pi - \\alpha_i) + 2 \\sum_{1 &lt; j &lt; n} \\cos (\\alpha_j - 0) + 2 \\sum_{2 \\le i &lt; j \\le n-1} \\cos (\\alpha_j - \\alpha_i) =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"841\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea191031688cc6cbeb568c236a326e1b64c3dbdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= T(\\alpha_2, \\dots, \\alpha_{n-1}) - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>In short, we showed that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880be0e8a609d47cfcbff39021cd6c27dd233241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) \\ge T(\\alpha_2, \\dots, \\alpha_{n-1}) - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460dce80925c74b24846b78ecf9505ac5edeb4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, and we apply this argument <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> times, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/5/9759b65ffcaf98886fa6d9e956e662cac40fb260.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) \\ge -2k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03d06f62dfaf2abf816dbac3ac90ea003b96a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) = n + T(\\alpha_1, \\dots, \\alpha_n) \\ge 2k + 1 - 2k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"423\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, May 2025]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we assume the plane to have the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> axis, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf281b877b370252c08b7774dbb0117f8036c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O = (0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />, and the vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e0c913f0bad8bed8a37b01168c6ecc9d631dce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"24\" /> to be pointed upwards. We will minimize\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a7cddf0cf6d2463d6279b5e222ff22f46bca12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Big|\\overrightarrow{OP_1} + \\cdots + \\overrightarrow{OP_n}\\Big|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"35\" />. Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/8232972ff6039695aeca6a7a60c32105af1d85a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\overrightarrow{O A_1} = \\overrightarrow{OP_2} + \\cdots + \\overrightarrow{OP_n}.\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"25\" />\nBy the law of cosines \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04be7a7141bff06ac90228997f0577c053baac5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big|\\overrightarrow{OP_1} + \\overrightarrow{O A_1} \\Big| = 1^2 + \\Big|\\overrightarrow{OA_1} \\Big|^2 - 2 \\Big|\\overrightarrow{OA_1} \\Big| \\cos(\\pi - \\phi_1)\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"36\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2629893cf0303c8874002b5502fc0c5f521810d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> is the (positive) angle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec9a264fd3be63037ee2bb8e88e4b90dc9b8365.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OA_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4b9c1f5ddf083a92bfa20138277ec5ccf8d465f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"24\" />. Apparently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> lies above the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> axis, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2629893cf0303c8874002b5502fc0c5f521810d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> is maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a364d616489f96d46f67daa36dbe03b5e6e6fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1} = (1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"25\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. By the above formula, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e5f2b15e15a70130dcee093fef0d355c060f58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\pi-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> is monotonically increasing on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece27ba559bd93cdf2416aa0f88fc8d7d85e5791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289653efe2eca3ff1ad4312b5786c396d6c6b353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Big|\\overrightarrow{OP_1} + \\overrightarrow{O A_1} \\Big|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"35\" /> is minimized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a364d616489f96d46f67daa36dbe03b5e6e6fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1} = (1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"25\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. Since we are trying to minimize \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf515fae113ac52591b640acd2dd2a407d1b8664.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big|\\overrightarrow{OP_1} + \\cdots + \\overrightarrow{OP_n}\\Big|\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"33\" />\nwe may now assume WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a364d616489f96d46f67daa36dbe03b5e6e6fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1} = (1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"25\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. Successively repeat this argument for the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> vectors (for instance taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028b9229bbc04cff9cc5716b0120112c6dd13803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_1}+\\overrightarrow{OP_3}+\\cdots+\\overrightarrow{OP_n} = \\overrightarrow{OA_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"251\" height=\"24\" /> to show WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da842a3c79cc7a2d5eb012667898ba472722d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_2} = (1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"25\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />) to get WLOG <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50b9fc8b2af759e4c74ef38d2d9d6e268fed940.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{OP_k} = (1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"25\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. At which point \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef335131089d31297cf4b01ac5f6096ff72a6046.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Big|\\overrightarrow{OP_1} + \\cdots +\\overrightarrow{OP_n}\\Big| = |m_1-m_2|\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"33\" /> \nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d659c8074c617549d61db9db0773e0fccad7b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of vectors equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee54e8432d4a60984309e86f32931b04c8e2f1da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of vectors equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b83617178c137c55232eea1ca6791131d94eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. Also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558a411781ce297ddf3d516cfb2e849a87a8a6ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1+m_2 = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" /> is odd. So that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/a/c4ae3042d0b758fa9d86d58112405191bab88dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|m_1-m_2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> clearly has minimum value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO\" title=\"1973 IMO\">1973 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017133239\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.059 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 849/100000